Hi Kenn,

Are you sure about the checksum for the 300 baud
format?  I know the 2000 baud recordings have one--a
beta version of Ballybin can even repair them (not
that it tends to help much; if the checksum and
program data don't match it probably means there was a
problem with the program data).  However, I've noticed
that loading a 2000 baud recording and a 300 baud
recording are quite different.  2000 baud loading is
all or nothing.  If you start in the middle,
AstroBASIC doesn't know what to do.  With a 300 baud
recording, you can start playing at any point and the
code will appear on the screen as it should.  Of
course, don't expect the program to work if you start
loading it in the middle.  :-)

Paul

